    <!-- Onboarding: battery -->
    <string name="onboarding_battery_hint_xiaomi">Xiaomi, Redmi and POCO: open App info, turn on Autostart, then set Battery saver to \"No restrictions\". Also lock Unscroll in the recent apps screen (pull its card down or long-press it).</string>
    <string name="onboarding_battery_hint_samsung">Samsung: go to Settings, then Battery, then Background usage limits. Remove Unscroll from \"Sleeping apps\" and \"Deep sleeping apps\", and add it to \"Never sleeping apps\".</string>
    <string name="onboarding_battery_hint_huawei">Huawei and Honor: go to Settings, then Battery, then App launch. Find Unscroll, switch it to \"Manage manually\" and turn on Auto-launch, Secondary launch and Run in background.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_battery_hint_oneplus">OnePlus: open App info, then Battery, and choose \"Allow background activity\" or \"Unrestricted\". Also lock Unscroll in the recent apps screen.</string>
    <string name="onboarding_battery_hint_other">Other phones can have their own battery savers. dontkillmyapp.com has steps for most brands.</string>

